    "report": "The notice of a new message now carries `listingId`. The work is committed on `main` as `5af3fda`, not pushed.\n\n**Checks:** typecheck, `test:units` (155 suites, 1049 tests), `test:e2e` (114 suites, 607 tests, including the Postgres notice path), `check:conventions`, `lint` and `format:check` all pass. I did not start a server.\n\n**Path of `listingId`:**\n- **Messaging:** `MessageSentEvent` records `listingId` in both `Conversation.start` and `Conversation.send`. `MessageSentHandler` passes it on.\n- **Shared kernel:** `MessageSentPayload` gains `listingId`. This is the contract between Messaging and Notifications.\n- **Notifications:** the handler maps it into `SentMessage`, and `MessageNoticeOwing` puts it on the notice. `MessageNoticeBody` gains the field.\n- **Persistence:** `notices.listing_id` already existed, so no migration. The message kind now writes and reads it.\n- **Delivery:** `NoticeDelivery` sends the body as-is, so the HTTP payload gains `listingId` with no change there.\n\nWho is told, how often, and the delivery and retry behaviour are untouched. Other notice kinds are unchanged.\n\n**Decisions and things to know:**\n- **Existing pending notices:** a message notice owed before this deploy and not yet accepted has no stored `listing_id`. It will go out with `listingId: null`. Backfilling would need Notifications to read Messaging's data, which crosses the context boundary, so I did not do it. If that matters, it needs a decision.\n- **Spec updates:** I added `listingId` to the existing message-notice expectations in unit and e2e specs. I did not add a new test asserting the listing id is the conversation's own listing.\n- **Architecture mode:** `yarn architecture mode feature` could not run, because it compares against `origin/main` and this repo has no such ref. I did not get its verdict on the `SharedKernel` change. The change is the contract field itself, which is the intended place for it.\n- **Docs:** ADR 57 and the message-notices storm still describe the old body. I left them alone.\n- **Branch:** I committed on `main` because you asked for the current branch. The git guidance in this session says to branch first when on the default branch, so say if you wanted a feature branch.",
